* Project Overview

The AI Agent Feedback Form is an intelligent automation workflow built using n8n, designed to manage and categorize user feedback automatically.
When a user submits feedback through a form, the system uses an AI Agent (OpenAI Chat Model) to analyze the message and classify it into predefined categories such as Complaint, Compliment, or Feature Request.

Once classified, the workflow automatically performs actions like:

* Creating records in Airtable for organized data storage

* Sending instant notifications to the team on Slack

* Sending acknowledgment or alert emails through Gmail

This eliminates manual sorting, improves response efficiency, and ensures that every feedback item is routed to the right department.

* Workflow Step 
** On Form Submission ** 

The workflow begins when a user submits the Feedback Form.
This trigger node collects the input data (name, email, and feedback message).

** AI Agent Processing ** 

The collected feedback is passed to an AI Agent node connected to the OpenAI Chat Model.
The AI analyzes the feedback content and predicts whether it’s a:
* Complaint 
* Compliment 
* Feature Addition Request 

** Merge Node **

The output from the AI Agent is merged with the original form data.
This ensures the system has both the feedback content and AI classification result in one combined dataset.

** Switch Node (Routing) **

The Switch node checks the AI’s classification and routes the data into one of three paths:
* Complaint
* Compliment
* Feature Addition Request

** Airtable Integration **

Each category of feedback creates a new record in the respective Airtable table:
* Complaints Table – logs issues or negative feedback
* Compliments Table – stores positive comments
* Feature Requests Table – captures new feature ideas

** Slack Notification **

A Slack message is sent to the appropriate team channel:
* Support team for complaints
* Product team for feature requests
* General or HR team for compliments
This ensures immediate visibility and faster response.


** Gmail Notification ** 

If the feedback type is Complaint, the workflow sends an automatic email (via Gmail node) to the user who submitted the form.
The email includes:
* A thank-you message for their feedback
* A note confirming their complaint has been received
* Optional tracking ID or contact information

** Workflow Completion **

The workflow ends after sending Slack and email notifications.
All feedback is logged and categorized automatically in Airtable.

** Tools Used ** 

** n8n **
** Open AI Chat Model **
** Airtable **
** Slack **
** Gmail **

** USE CASE **
Automatically classify and route complaints to the right support staff.
Send acknowledgment emails to customers confirming receipt.
Capture feature requests and log them in Airtable for review.
Notify product managers via Slack when new ideas arrive

** Workflow Outcome **

* Feedback is instantly analyzed by AI and sorted into categories.
* All submissions are stored neatly in Airtable for tracking and analysis.
* Real-time Slack notifications alert the correct teams to take quick action.
* Users who submit complaints receive an automatic confirmation email.
* Structured feedback helps teams identify common issues and opportunities.
* Entire process — from collection to notification — runs without human intervention.





